    "note": "Note to Teachers about Shifts in Content Organization In previous grade levels, history guidelines are outlined for both World and American History. This organization shifts in grades 7–8. Here, each grade level offers either a survey of American history or a survey of World history. This intentional design affords two key benefits. First, it offers students the opportunity to expand their knowledge and apply higher levels of analysis to previously taught topics. They can explore new perspectives, uncover novel detail, and come to recognize shades of nuance. This new knowledge not only leads to greater understanding, it also draws lines of sight between the past and present. The second benefit of this design is that it affords educators more flexibility. For example, schools can:",
